// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 15-function-semantics
// facility: [Closure-Form-Borrow] (spec/15 §6; CHG-0439): a capture without `move` destroyed in the body; conf.borrow-capture-dropped
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.destroy-while-aliased (static)
//
// `[s]` borrows `s` while the closure runs; the body cannot destroy it.
// Both tools faulted when it ran, under different diagnostics.

import std;

fn main()
{
    String s = "a";
    auto f = [s]()
    {
        drop(s);
    };
    f();
}
